    "contrast": "pretrain_probe_capturable ran the SAME architecture, corpus and shapes through a HAND-WRITTEN XLA loop and recompiled every step. The only variable changed here is who owns the training loop.",
    "tokens_per_step_note": "seq_len * micro_batch * grad_accum * dp_size, with dp_size=1. Data parallelism is the ONLY dimension that multiplies tokens: tensor parallelism shards one model across cores working on the SAME micro-batch, so tp=1 multiplies neither the batch nor the token count. optimum-neuron 0.4.3 exposes no data-parallel dimension at all -- NeuronTrainingArguments builds its world as tp x pp -- so dp is 1 in every lane here and the multiplier is 1.",
    "confound_vs_hand_written_loop": "This lane is NOT a clean one-variable comparison against pretrain_probe_capturable. That lane ran DP=2 on both NeuronCores under a hand-written loop; this one runs on 1 core(s) at tp=1 under NeuronTrainer. Loop ownership AND the parallelism layout both changed. A successful run here shows the FRAMEWORK path works; it does not by itself prove the hand-written loop was the cause of the per-step recompile. Closing that would need the hand loop re-run at nproc=1. Flagged by an independent reviewer; recorded rather than glossed.",
    "note_plain_torch_xla_does_support_dp2": "Worth separating: the HAND-WRITTEN lane really did run DP=2 across both cores under plain torchrun + torch_xla. The missing data-parallel dimension is a property of optimum-neuron 0.4.3's NeuronTrainingArguments, NOT of Trainium or of torch_xla."
